# Pre-push gate overrides for skills (consumed by atlas/scripts/test-project.sh)

# Lint gate held OFF — named debt, not a silent skip.
#
# Until 2026-08-02 this repo typed as `unknown` (no pyproject.toml / ruff.toml /
# requirements.txt), so the pre-push gate printed "skipping verification" and
# exited 0 on every push. That is an inert gate wearing a green face — see
# atlas/patterns/check-liveness-proof.md. Detection now recognizes tracked *.py,
# so the gate is real; this file records that we are choosing not to arm it yet
# rather than pretending it was never there.
#
# Measured 2026-08-02 with the pinned ruff (atlas/templates/ruff-pin.txt, 0.16.1)
# over tracked *.py only:
#
#   12 tracked .py — 356 violations
#     UP006 178 · BLE001 38 · UP045 37 · RUF013 23 · UP035 21
#
# NOTE ON REMEDIATION: ruff 0.16.1 ships a very broad default rule set (413
# rules), so most of this is stylistic modernization, not correctness — UP006
# alone (use `list` not `List`) is half the count here. The right fix is usually
# to add a ruff.toml SELECTING the rules this repo wants, then delete this line
# — not to grind through the raw count.
SKIP_LINT=true
